          <item>
    <title>We crossed into Ecuador today</title>
    <link>https://hobobiker-prep.ddev.site/node/4155</link>
    <description>&lt;div class=&quot;flickrfloat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;flickrfloat&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;flickr-img-wrapper&quot;&gt;
        &lt;a rel=&quot;lightbox[group1][]&quot; href=&quot;/sites/default/files/2531763703_Nancy_and_Randy_at_the_Ecuador_border.jpg&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://hobobiker-prep.ddev.site/sites/default/files/imagecache/240x180/2531763703_Nancy_and_Randy_at_the_Ecuador_border.jpg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; title=&quot;&quot; rel=&quot;lightbox[group1][]&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;        &lt;/a&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We crossed into Ecuador today! Our 10th country. 11,000 miles (17,700 km) into the ride. It&#039;s high, cold, mountainous. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the last few days we&#039;ve been riding up to and above 10,000 feet in elevation and it&#039;s been so cloudy or foggy that we can&#039;t see much at all of the beautiful scenery above us. We can usually see valleys below, but can&#039;t see even the sides of the great volcanoes.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
